    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract concepts and real-world problem-solving. While my parents didn’t push me toward it much (my dad was more into history), I find its logic intriguing—almost like solving puzzles where every equation has a hidden meaning. It’s not just about memorizing formulas but understanding *why* things work, which aligns with how I enjoy exploring physics and biology in school.",
